From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wldap32: no host name is the default host, not an unterminated URL

ldap_init(""), ldap_open("") and ldap_sslinit("") -- no host name, or only
blanks -- split into no host names at all; joining them computed a size of
(0 - 1) separators, allocated zero bytes and returned that block, never
terminated, as the URL. ldap_initialize then parsed whatever the heap held:
usually a session for nothing, sometimes LDAP_URL_ERR and no session.

Microsoft Word calls ldap_initW(L"", 3268) (the global catalog of the
machine's domain) seconds after it starts. When the call failed, Word wrote
through a NULL pointer (0xc0000005) and its crash handler ended the process
(0xe0000002, then the "Word couldn't start last time" prompt). On a busy
machine it happened often enough to look like Word "crashing at random",
including while saving.

No host name now means the default host, as a NULL host name already did
(localhost; Windows asks its domain's directory). Gate: test-ldapemptyhost
(heap checking makes the old URL fail every time); mutant
SG_MUTANT_EMPTY_HOST_UNTERMINATED fails it.
---
--- a/dlls/wldap32/init.c
+++ b/dlls/wldap32/init.c
@@ -180,12 +180,18 @@
 static char *urlify_hostnames( const char *scheme, char *hostnames, ULONG port )
 {
     char *url = NULL, **strarray;
+    static char localhost[] = "localhost";
+    char *default_host[] = { localhost, NULL };
 
     strarray = split_hostnames( hostnames );
-    if (strarray)
-        url = join_hostnames( scheme, strarray, port );
-    else
-        return NULL;
+    if (!strarray) return NULL;
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_EMPTY_HOST_UNTERMINATED
+    url = join_hostnames( scheme, strarray, port );
+#else
+    /* no host name at all ("" or only blanks) is the default host, as NULL
+     * is; joining no names gave a zero-byte, unterminated URL */
+    url = join_hostnames( scheme, strarray[0] ? strarray : default_host, port );
+#endif
 
     strarrayfreeU( strarray );
     return url;
